## 1. The source differential is simpler than its projection

Let `A` be the exterior differential graded algebra on three degree-one
generators `a,b,c`:

```text
d a=0,
d b=0,
d c=a wedge b.
```

This is the Chevalley-Eilenberg algebra of the three-dimensional Heisenberg/Nil
Lie algebra. The only contractible pair is

```text
c -> a wedge b.
```

Its cohomology has representatives

```text
H=span(1,a,b,a wedge c,b wedge c,a wedge b wedge c).
```

Define inclusion `i`, projection `p`, and homotopy `h` by

```text
h(a wedge b)=c,
h=0 on every other basis monomial.
```

Then

```text
d h+h d=id-i p,
p i=id_H,
h^2=p h=h i=0.
```

## 2. Transferred products

The homological perturbation theorem transfers the DGA product to an
`A_infinity` structure on `H`. At the first two nontrivial levels, use the
convention

```text
m2(x,y)=p(i x wedge i y),

m3(x,y,z)
 =p(
      h(i x wedge i y) wedge i z
      -(-1)^|x| i x wedge h(i y wedge i z)
    ).
```

### Theorem 2.1

The transferred ternary product is nonzero. In particular,

```text
m3(a,a,b)=a wedge c,
m3(a,b,b)=-b wedge c.
```

### Proof

For the first identity, `a wedge a=0`, while

```text
h(a wedge b)=c.
```

Because `|a|=1`, the second tree enters with a plus sign and yields
`a wedge c`. For the second identity, the first tree gives
`c wedge b=-b wedge c`, while `b wedge b=0`. QED.

With the displayed cohomological sign convention, the resulting `m2,m3`
satisfy the arity-four Stasheff identity. The verifier checks that identity on
all `6^4=1296` homogeneous cohomology-basis quadruples.

Thus projection can turn one binary preprojection relation, `dc=ab`, into a
genuine ternary postprojection operation. A complicated lower interaction need
not be a separate primitive.

## 3. Shared-line equivariance

Assign integer circle weights

```text
w(a)=1,
w(b)=1,
w(c)=2.
```

The relation `dc=ab` is homogeneous because

```text
w(c)=w(a)+w(b).
```

The product, differential, projection, inclusion, and homotopy all preserve
weight. Consequently every transferred operation preserves total weight. The
same statement descends modulo three to a `Z3` character:

```text
w(a)=w(b)=1,
w(c)=2 mod 3.
```

For example, the input and output weights of `m3(a,a,b)=ac` are both zero
modulo three.

This supplies an exact structural relation among:

```text
shared circle weight
  -> finite Lens/Z3 character
  -> Heisenberg-Nil differential
  -> transferred higher interaction.
```

It does not prove that the selected MTT shared line has these weights.

## 4. Central persistent curvature

Adjoin a central even curvature

```text
m0=lambda 1.
```

It is closed, harmonic, annihilated by `h`, and commutes with the entire DGA.
The contraction preserves the unit and is strictly unital, so the central
curved-DGA datum survives the displayed contraction as

```text
m0_H=lambda 1_H
```

without curving the adjoint differential; higher operations vanish whenever a
unit is inserted. Its Jordan action remains nonzero. This is an explicit
strictly unital realization of the central-curvature regime.

General noncentral curvature requires the full curved homological perturbation
series and its convergence or nilpotent-filtration hypotheses. That step is not
claimed here.

